# Random Password Generator (Python, Advanced GUI Tier)

A tkinter GUI tool that generates strong, cryptographically secure passwords
based on user-defined criteria.

## Features

- GUI with a length spinbox and checkboxes for character type selection
- Uses Python's `secrets` module (not `random`) — cryptographically secure
- Guarantees at least one character from each selected type
- Password strength indicator: Weak / Medium / Strong
- "Copy to Clipboard" button via `pyperclip`
- Option to exclude ambiguous characters (`0`, `O`, `l`, `1`, `I`)
- Session-only history of the last 5 generated passwords (kept in memory
  only — never written to disk, for security)
- Input validation: minimum 8-character length, at least 2 character types

## Tech Stack

- Python 3
- tkinter (GUI)
- secrets (cryptographically secure random generation)
- pyperclip (clipboard access)

## Setup

```bash
pip install pyperclip
```

## Run

```bash
python password_generator.py
```

Choose a length (8–64), pick at least two character types, optionally
exclude ambiguous characters, then click **Generate Password**.

## Security Notes

- Uses `secrets.choice()` and `secrets.randbelow()` throughout — the same
  module recommended by the Python docs for anything security-sensitive,
  instead of the non-cryptographic `random` module.
- The password history is intentionally not persisted to any file, so a
  generated password never lingers on disk after you close the app.
